SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE

This MIT license covers the port's own material in this directory: the build
and launcher scripts, the test reproducer, the documentation, and the patch
files as authored works.

It does NOT relicense the projects being patched. When a patch is applied, the
resulting modified files remain under their upstream licenses:

  - tailscale/tailscale ......... BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) Tailscale Inc &
                                  contributors. See the LICENSE file in the
                                  tailscale repository. Files added by
                                  patches/0001-tailscale-haiku386.patch carry
                                  Tailscale's SPDX headers and are contributed
                                  under that same license.
  - The Go programming language . BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) The Go Authors.
                                  The go-runtime/*.patch files modify Go's
                                  runtime; the modified files stay under Go's
                                  license.
  - gvisor, wireguard-go ........ their own licenses (Apache-2.0 and
                                  BSD-3-Clause respectively).

In short: the glue is MIT, the patched code keeps its upstream license.
